# OpenEVV sound map: Myanmar (Burmese) (eSpeak NG voice sit/my), spoken by openevv's German module
# with the sounds, the melody and the tones of the language itself.
# Written by engine/accent/mapwriter.py; OpenEvvFrontend reads it, and docs/LANGUAGES.md
# says what each line means. Edit freely: the file is read each time a voice starts.

template dedx
style standard
vowels i I e E a A u U o O y Y oe OE @ aj aw oj a~ E~ o~ oe~ E: R
glides j w
schwa @
secondary 2
words apart
onset 2

# the melody: tone; a question that wants yes or no: fall
accent f0=own range=100 level=30 decl=6 declmax=25 lag=70 lead=15 fs=-6 fq=6 qreg=18 fc=4 fe=0 fw=-4 span=1 stressed=94 weak=106 stop=1

# the tones, under eSpeak NG's names for them
tone 1 p=0:12,80:12,100:16 dur=105
tone 2 p=0:47,70:50,100:34 dur=115 brth=15
tone 3 p=0:52,100:30 dur=72 creak=60 cfrom=40 cto=100 stop=25
tone 4 p=0:50,100:47 dur=48 stop=40

# what the module says in place of a phone it is given
says C t S
says J d Z
says P p f
says T t s

